---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

export const prerender = true;

---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses and protects your information.`}
  lede="What this site stores in your browser and what outside services may receive."
  updated="November 7, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {SITE.name} ("we", "us") handles information when you visit
    <strong>{SITE.url}</strong>. We have tried to write it in plain language. If anything is
    unclear, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Information and browser storage</h2>
  <p>There is no account system or login on this site.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Messages you send.</strong> If you use the contact form or email us directly, we
      receive your name, email address and the information in your message. If the form is handled
      by a form-delivery service, that service processes the message on our behalf only to deliver
      it to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Saved ideas and reading preferences.</strong> The save buttons and text-size control
      store post IDs and your selected text size in your browser's local storage. This information
      stays in that browser and is not sent to us. You can clear it through your browser settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical request data.</strong> Our hosting provider may process information such as
      your IP address, browser, and requested page to deliver and protect the site. The provider's
      own retention and security practices also apply.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Outside services.</strong> The site loads a Google Analytics 4 tag to measure visits.
      In the EEA, the UK and Switzerland it sets no analytics cookies until you agree, though Google
      may still receive limited signals; elsewhere it uses cookies to count visits and page views.
      The site shows ads through Google AdSense, and Google and its partners use
      cookies or similar technologies as described below. The site also loads Pinterest's sharing script;
      Pinterest may process information under its own
      <a href="https://policy.pinterest.com/privacy-policy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The site does not currently offer an email newsletter signup or collect payment details.</p>
  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To operate, maintain, and protect the site.</li>
    <li>To understand site usage through Google Analytics, subject to the consent settings in use.</li>
    <li>To reply to messages you send us directly.</li>
    <li>To display advertising through Google AdSense, which pays for the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    This site displays ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its advertising partners use
    cookies, web beacons, IP addresses, or similar identifiers to serve, measure, and personalise
    ads. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits
    to this website and to other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its
    partners to serve ads to you based on those visits. Google explains
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">how it uses data on partner sites</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>,
    or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  {SITE.monetagDirectLink && (
    <>
      <h2>Sponsored links</h2>
      <p>
        The site footer carries a link marked <strong>Sponsored offers</strong>, supplied by Monetag.
        It is an ordinary link: nothing from Monetag loads on this site, and nothing is stored in your
        browser until you choose to follow it. If you do, you leave this site for an offer selected by
        Monetag, and that site's own privacy practices apply. We do not choose, review or endorse the
        offers shown, and we may earn a payment when the link is used.
      </p>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files a website or a third party stores in your browser. This site and the
    services it uses may set the following:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Strictly necessary / local storage</strong> — your saved ideas and text-size choice, kept only in your browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</strong> — cookies such as <code>_ga</code> that measure visits and page views, only where analytics storage is permitted.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising (Google AdSense and its partners)</strong> — cookies such as <code>__gads</code>, <code>__gpi</code> and <code>IDE</code> used to serve, cap, measure and, where permitted, personalise ads.</li>
    <li><strong>Pinterest</strong> — cookies set by Pinterest's save-button script.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking advertising cookies does not
    stop ads from showing, but they will be less relevant to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="consent">Consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>
    For visitors in these regions, advertising and analytics consent starts at denied. They are
    shown Google's consent message, a consent management platform certified under the IAB
    Transparency and Consent Framework, and nothing that needs consent is used until you choose.
    You can change that choice at any time with the <strong>Privacy settings</strong> link in the
    footer of every page. For any other question about consent, contact
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. Information may be processed by:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> — analytics signals, and advertising delivery and measurement through AdSense.</li>
    <li><strong>Our hosting provider (Vercel)</strong> — to serve and protect the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Google advertising partners</strong> — third-party ad vendors that Google certifies. Google lists them in its <a href="https://support.google.com/admanager/answer/9012903" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">ad technology providers list</a>.</li>
    {SITE.monetagDirectLink && (
      <li><strong>Monetag</strong> — only if you follow the footer's sponsored link, and then on Monetag's own site rather than this one.</li>
    )}
    <li><strong>Pinterest</strong> — when its sharing script is loaded or you use a Pinterest link.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal authorities</strong> — where we are legally required to.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Legal bases (GDPR and UK GDPR)</h2>
  <p>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, we rely on:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> — for analytics and advertising cookies, and for personalised ads. You can withdraw consent at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — to operate, secure and improve the site, and to reply to messages you send.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — where we must keep or disclose information by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some providers, including Google, may process data outside your country. Where they do, they
    rely on safeguards such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses or the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, privacy laws may give you rights to access, correct, or delete
    personal information we hold about you, or to object to certain uses of it.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>EEA and UK residents</strong> have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict or port their data, to object to processing, to withdraw consent, and to complain to their local data protection authority.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>California residents (CCPA/CPRA)</strong> have the right to know what personal
      information is collected, to delete it, to correct it, and to opt out of its "sale" or
      "sharing" for cross-context behavioural advertising. We do not sell personal information for
      money. Advertising cookies may count as "sharing" under California law; you can opt out using
      the browser controls above, a Global Privacy Control signal, or by emailing us. We will not
      treat you differently for exercising these rights.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We will respond
    within any period required by applicable law and handle other requests as promptly as practical.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and security</h2>
  <p>
    We retain direct email messages for as long as needed to handle the conversation and meet our
    legal obligations. Saved ideas and reading preferences remain in your browser until you clear
    its local storage. The site is served over HTTPS. No method of transmission over the internet
    is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is written for adults and is not directed at children under 13 (or under 16 in the
    EEA and UK). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a
    child has sent us information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when our practices change. The date at the top shows when this page
    was last revised.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

</PageLayout>
